      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nXPU on main is broken. This PR fixes `greedy_argmax`'s torch fallback to treat NaNs as `-inf`, matching its documented contract and Triton path. This issue was introduced by #57770.\r\n\r\n**Notes for Reviewers**\r\n\r\n- The fix only touches the torch fallback, which runs on XPU, for fp16, and for small vocabularies. The Triton path that bf16/fp32 models use on CUDA and ROCm is unchanged, so typical deployments see no difference.\r\n- The trade-off is one extra copy of the logits on the fallback path. That's a small cost next to the weights the draft step already reads, and it's the price of getting the same token for the same logits everywhere.\r\n- Turning on the Triton kernel for XPU would avoid that copy, but it needs XPU performance numbers and sign-off from the XPU owners. CPU and non-contiguous inputs would still need this fallback anyway. I kept this PR to the minimal fix so XPU CI is unblocked, and we can address the Triton change in a follow up PR.\r\n- Why not just fix the test? The docstring already promises NaN is treated as -inf, and the Triton path does exactly that. Changing the test instead would let the drafted token depend on the platform and dtype.\r\n\r\n## Reproducer\r\n\r\nAdd `1000` to the existing test's vocab parameters, then run the same command before and after the fallback fix:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n  python -m pytest -v \\\r\n  tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_gumbel_sample.py -k test_greedy_argmax_matches_torch\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Output on main / on branch\r\n\r\nH100 80GB, PyTorch 2.14.0+cu130, Triton 3.8.0. Main's two new fallback cases fail at the NaN row; all six Triton cases pass.\r\n\r\n```text\r\nMain + test parameter:\r\n============ 2 failed, 6 passed, 22 deselected, 1 warning in 3.69s =============\r\nBranch:\r\n================= 8 passed, 22 deselected, 1 warning in 2.92s ==================\r\nFull file on branch:\r\n======================== 30 passed, 1 warning in 18.08s ========================\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nThe `:intel: (BMG) V1 test` in CI verifies these failures are cleared and the suite reaches later tests. \r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Implementation and environment</summary>\r\n\r\nThe fallback uses `masked_fill(isnan, -inf).argmax(-1)`, preserving infinities and first-index ties without modifying inputs. It adds a mask and logits copy only on the fallback. The Triton kernels and gating are unchanged, so eligible BF16/FP32 CUDA/ROCm inputs keep the existing execution path.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## AI assistance disclosure\r\n\r\nCodex (GPT-6) helped draft  this change.\r\n",
